{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst long long MOD = 1000000007LL;\n\nlong long powMod(long long x, long long y) {\n    long long ans = 1;\n    while (y) {\n        if (y & 1LL) ans = (ans * x) % MOD;\n        x = (x * x) % MOD;\n        y >>= 1LL;\n    }\n    return ans;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int P, K;\n    scanf(\"%d%d\", &P, &K);\n\n    vector<int> parent(P, 0), rnk(P, 0);\n    for (int i = 1; i < P; ++i) {\n        parent[i] = i;\n        rnk[i] = 1;\n    }\n\n    auto find = [&](int x) {\n        while (parent[x] != x) {\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]];\n            x = parent[x];\n        }\n        return x;\n    };\n\n    auto unite = [&](int a, int b) {\n        if (rnk[a] >= rnk[b]) {\n            parent[b] = a;\n            ++rnk[a];\n        } else {\n            parent[a] = b;\n            ++rnk[b];\n        }\n    };\n\n    for (int i = 1; i < P; ++i) {\n        int v = (int)((long long)K * i % P);\n        int a = find(i);\n        int b = find(v);\n        if (a != b)\n            unite(a, b);\n    }\n\n    vector<char> isRoot(P, 0);\n    int groupCount = 0;\n    for (int i = 1; i < P; ++i) {\n        int r = find(i);\n        if (!isRoot[r]) {\n            isRoot[r] = 1;\n            ++groupCount;\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long ways;\n    if (K == 0)\n        ways = powMod(P, P - 1);\n    else if (K == 1)\n        ways = powMod(P, P);\n    else\n        ways = powMod(P, groupCount);\n\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", ways);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef pow_mod(x, y):\n    ans = 1\n    while y:\n        if y & 1:\n            ans = (ans * x) % MOD\n        x = (x * x) % MOD\n        y >>= 1\n    return ans\n\ndef main():\n    import sys\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    P, K = map(int, data[:2])\n\n    parent = [0] * P\n    rnk = [0] * P\n    for i in range(1, P):\n        parent[i] = i\n        rnk[i] = 1\n\n    def find(x):\n        while parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\n            x = parent[x]\n        return x\n\n    def unite(a, b):\n        if rnk[a] >= rnk[b]:\n            parent[b] = a\n            rnk[a] += 1\n        else:\n            parent[a] = b\n            rnk[b] += 1\n\n    for i in range(1, P):\n        v = (K * i) % P\n        a = find(i)\n        b = find(v)\n        if a != b:\n            unite(a, b)\n\n    is_root = [False] * P\n    group_count = 0\n    for i in range(1, P):\n        r = find(i)\n        if not is_root[r]:\n            is_root[r] = True\n            group_count += 1\n\n    if K == 0:\n        ways = pow_mod(P, P - 1)\n    elif K == 1:\n        ways = pow_mod(P, P)\n    else:\n        ways = pow_mod(P, group_count)\n\n    print(ways)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-4.577532e-05, 0.0, -5.960463e-07, -0.00150829, -0.07099344, -1.